/-
# Relatively free groups with nilpotent subsets (Kourovka Notebook Problem 8.56)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.56 (A. Yu. Olshanskii): let `X` be a finite
set and `f` a mapping from the set of subsets of `X` to the positive integers. Under the requirement
that in a group generated by `X`, every subgroup `⟨Y⟩`, `Y ⊆ X`, be nilpotent of class `≤ f(Y)`, is
it true that the free group `G_f` relative to this condition is torsion-free?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Nilpotent

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.RelativelyFreeNilpotentSubsetsTorsionKourovka8Problem56Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.56 (A. Yu.
Olshanskii). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700506 (`KOU-8.56`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`G_f` is the free group on `X` modulo the normal closure of the terms `γ_{f(Y)+1}⟨Y⟩` of the lower
central series of the subgroups `⟨Y⟩` (Mathlib's `Subgroup.lowerCentralSeries`, whose term `c` is
`γ_{c+1}`); it is the universal group generated by `X` in which each `⟨Y⟩` is nilpotent of class at
most `f(Y)`. Torsion-free means no non-trivial element of finite order.
-/

/-- The relations of `G_f`: the normal closure in the free group on `X` of the terms
`γ_{f(Y)+1}⟨Y⟩` of the lower central series of the subgroups `⟨Y⟩`, `Y ⊆ X`
(`(closure Y).lowerCentralSeries c` is `γ_{c+1}⟨Y⟩`). -/
abbrev nilpotencyRelations {X : Type} (f : Set X → ℕ) : Subgroup (FreeGroup X) :=
  Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ Y : Set X,
    ((Subgroup.closure (FreeGroup.of '' Y)).lowerCentralSeries (f Y) : Set (FreeGroup X)))

/-- The free group `G_f` relative to the condition that every subgroup `⟨Y⟩`, `Y ⊆ X`, be
nilpotent of class at most `f Y`. -/
abbrev relativelyFreeGroup (X : Type) (f : Set X → ℕ) : Type :=
  FreeGroup X ⧸ nilpotencyRelations f

/-- Kourovka 8.56 (A. Yu. Olshanskii): for every finite set `X` and every `f` from the subsets of
`X` to the positive integers, the group `G_f` is torsion-free. -/
def relativelyFreeGroupTorsionFree : Prop :=
  ∀ (X : Type) [Finite X] (f : Set X → ℕ), (∀ Y, 0 < f Y) →
    ∀ g : relativelyFreeGroup X f, g ≠ 1 → ¬ IsOfFinOrder g

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 8.56 "Not always", citing Bludov, Kleimenov and
Khlamov, Counterexample to a question of A. Yu. Ol'shanskii (1990). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D.
Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.56 (A. Yu. Olshanskii); resolution:
V. V. Bludov, V. F. Kleimenov and E. V. Khlamov, Counterexample to a question of A. Yu. Ol'shanskii,
Algebra and Logic 29 (1990), 95-96, Kourovka Archive, Problem 8.56: Not always (Bludov, Kleimenov
and Khlamov), https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02001354.
-/
public theorem_wanted relativelyFreeGroupTorsionFree_refuted : ¬ relativelyFreeGroupTorsionFree

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.RelativelyFreeNilpotentSubsetsTorsionKourovka8Problem56Wanted
